    "updated_at": "2026-09-14T22:05:38Z",
    "body": "Historical review found that Docker was not a Rung artifact dependency, but the retired public web-serving path did use Docker Compose + Cloudflare Tunnel on the operator host (sf0.5 PRD-006 and INC-107 evidence). This increment adds a release-path guard that checks executable release metadata/scripts for container-runtime markers while allowing the existing Docker-socket security prohibition. Local validation: 64 tests passed, standalone artifact check passed, distribution contract passed, and full validate_release.py --dist dist passed. Direct main push was rejected by repository rules; change is being sent through a PR. Push blocker 5-Whys: main rejected because rules require PR; PR requires audit; audit is the repository trust gate; bypassing it would weaken the release boundary; therefore no bypass is authorized.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
